    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Die Ruinen von Nuestra Señora de Santa Ana gehören zu den jesuitischen Guaraní-Reduktionen in der Provinz Misiones. 1633 von Pater Pedro de Oñate gegründet, war die Mission ein Modell der Selbstversorgung, in dem spanische Jesuiten und indigene Guaraní gemeinsam lebten und arbeiteten. Die monumentale Kirche aus rotem Sandstein, die Werkstätten und der einzigartige Steinkreuzweg zeugen vom hohen architektonischen und sozialen Niveau. Nach der Vertreibung der Jesuiten 1767 durch König Karl III. verfiel die Mission. Seit 1984 zählt sie zum UNESCO-Welterbe und gilt als Mahnmal jenes außergewöhnlichen kulturellen Experiments im kolonialen Río de la Plata.",
      en: "The ruins of Nuestra Señora de Santa Ana are part of the Jesuit Missions of the Guaranis, located in the lush Misiones Province. Founded in the 17th century, the mission was a self-sufficient community where Jesuit priests and indigenous Guaraní people lived and worked together. The site features the remains of a monumental church, workshops, residences, and a cemetery, all built with characteristic reddish sandstone. Santa Ana is particularly notable for its impressive stone carvings and its unique cemetery that remained in use long after the mission was abandoned. Today, the ruins are a UNESCO World Heritage site, surrounded by recovering rainforest, offering a hauntingly beautiful testimony to the complex social and religious experiment that defined the colonial era in the Upper Paraná region.",
      hu: "Nuestra Se?ora de Santa Ana a jezsuita misszi?romok egyik csendes, erd?vel k?rbevett helysz?ne Misiones tartományban. A telep a 17. században a guaran? k?z?ss?gek ?s a jezsuit?k egy?ttm?k?d?s?re ?p?lt, vagyis egyszerre volt vallási központ, mez?gazdasági telep ?s szervezett lak?hely. Ma a falmaradv?nyok, az alaprajz ?s a templom k?rny?ke mutatja meg, hogyan m?k?d?tt egy redukci? a gyarmati korban. A hely a világ?r?ks?gi sorozat r?sze, ?s j?l ?érzékelteti, hogy a misszi?k nem elszigetelt pontok, hanem egymással ?sszekapcsolt h?l?zatot alkottak.",
      ro: "Misiunea Nuestra Señora de Santa Ana a fost una dintre numeroasele așezări fondate de ordinul iezuit în secolul al XVII-lea pentru a evangheliza populația Guarani. Situată în provincia Misiones, ruinele sale actuale oferă o imagine impresionantă a structurii urbanistice iezuite, incluzând resturile bisericii, ale pieței centrale și ale locuințelor indigene. Fondată inițial în 1633, misiunea a trebuit să fie relocată de mai multe ori din cauza atacurilor bandeiirantes. Arhitectura combină stilul baroc european cu motive decorative locale executate de artiști Guarani în gresie roșie. Abandonată după expulzarea iezuiților în 1767, natura a invadat treptat structurile, creând un peisaj melancolic și fascinant care a fost inclus în patrimoniul UNESCO în 1984."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      de: ["1633 von den Jesuiten unter Pater Pedro de Oñate gegründet.", "1984 als Teil der Jesuitenmissionen zum UNESCO-Welterbe erklärt.", "Nach der Vertreibung der Jesuiten 1767 verlassen.", "Beherbergt einen einzigartigen Kreuzweg (via crucis) aus Stein.", "Der Friedhof wurde bis Mitte des 20. Jahrhunderts genutzt.", "Verfügte über ein fortschrittliches Bewässerungssystem.", "Erbaut aus rotem Sandstein der Region (asperón colorado).", "Liegt nur wenige Kilometer vom heutigen Ort Santa Ana entfernt."],
      en: ["Founded in 1633 by the Jesuits.", "Part of a group of missions declared UNESCO World Heritage in 1984.", "The church's facade was once one of the most ornate in the region.", "Home to a unique 'way of the cross' (via crucis) built in stone.", "The cemetery was used by local settlers until the mid-20th century.", "Features an advanced irrigation and water distribution system.", "Surrounded by a protected botanical reserve.", "Located just a few kilometers from the town of Santa Ana."],
